insert into public.navi_knowledge (question, answer, category) values
('What is included in the Seller plan?', 'The Seller plan is free forever. It includes: VAT/VIES-verified company listing, publishing CBAM and GO surplus certificates, automatic view counter, email inquiry alerts, and EFET contract template on match. No subscription, no commitment.', 'pricing'),
('What does PRO Compliance include?', 'PRO Compliance (79 €/month or 790 €/year) includes everything in Seller plus: CBAM & ETS calculator for all Annex I sectors, compliance dashboard, regulatory change alerts, email support, multi-shipment CBAM planner, supplier emissions request tool, XML & PDF export in EU CBAM format, CBAM declaration builder, and AI cost forecast.', 'pricing'),
('What does PRO Trading include?', 'PRO Trading (249 €/month or 2,490 €/year) includes everything in PRO Compliance plus: ETS cost tracker with real-time prices, OTC bulletin board for CBAM and GO certificates, match alerts and MSR notifications, EU Sanctions screening via VIES, EFET contract generation, and priority support.', 'pricing'),
('Is there an early bird offer?', 'Yes — the first 10 companies get PRO Trading at 1,990 €/year instead of 2,490 €/year. That is a 500 € saving, locked in permanently as long as you stay subscribed. Starts with a 30-day free trial.', 'pricing'),
('How do I start a free trial?', 'Go to carbonis.eu/register and create your account. No credit card required. Your 30-day trial gives you full PRO Compliance access. You choose your plan when the trial ends.', 'onboarding'),
('How does the multi-shipment CBAM planner work?', 'The multi-shipment planner lets you input up to 20 import shipments at once — each with a CN code, quantity, country of origin, and embedded CO2 value. It calculates your total annual CBAM liability and shows a certificate purchase timeline. Available in PRO Compliance and PRO Trading.', 'features'),
('How do I export a CBAM declaration as XML?', 'In your dashboard, go to the CBAM Declaration Builder, fill in all required fields, and click Export. You get an XML file in the official DG TAXUD format, ready to upload to the EU CBAM Registry. PDF export is also available for your records.', 'features'),
('What is the supplier emissions request tool?', 'It sends a standardised embedded emissions questionnaire to your suppliers by email. They fill it in, and the data comes back structured into your Carbonis dashboard — ready to import directly into your CBAM declaration. No manual data entry.', 'features'),
('What sectors does the CBAM calculator cover?', 'The calculator covers all six CBAM Annex I sectors: cement, iron and steel, aluminium, fertilisers, electricity, and hydrogen. A basic version is also available free at carbonis.eu/cbam.', 'features'),
('How does the OTC bulletin board work?', 'In PRO Trading, you can post buy or sell offers for CBAM certificates, Guarantees of Origin, and EUAs. Other verified members see your offer. When there is a match, both parties negotiate directly — no broker, no exchange fee. Carbonis generates the EFET contract automatically.', 'features'),
('What is an MSR alert?', 'MSR stands for Market Stability Reserve — an EU mechanism that removes ETS allowances from circulation when supply is too high. MSR interventions affect ETS certificate prices. PRO Trading members get alerts when MSR is triggered, helping them time their certificate purchases.', 'features'),
('How long is the free trial?', '30 days, full PRO Compliance access. No credit card required. You can cancel or choose a plan at any time during or after the trial.', 'onboarding'),
('Can I cancel my subscription?', 'Yes, you can cancel anytime. There are no lock-in contracts. If you cancel a monthly plan, access continues until the end of the billing period.', 'pricing'),
('How is billing handled?', 'Currently billing is handled manually via invoice (Xolo Go). Stripe subscription billing is coming soon. Contact info@carbonis.eu to start your plan after the free trial.', 'pricing'),
('Who is Carbonis for?', 'Carbonis serves three types of users: (1) Sellers — companies with surplus CBAM or GO certificates who want to find buyers for free. (2) Compliance teams — EU importers of Annex I goods who need to file CBAM declarations. (3) Traders — companies that actively buy and sell carbon certificates and need an OTC marketplace.', 'general');
